    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0812" n="662" xml:id="pg662"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6775/222.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the President of
                    Honduras.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November 16,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Acknowledging your gratifying telegram of the 13th, reporting the friendly
                    conference at Amapala, at which it was agreed to consider all differences among
                    the Governments of Honduras, Nicaragua, and Salvador at an end, I have the
                    pleasure to assure you of the cordial appreciation of the Government and people
                    of the United States of anything that may tend to the development of peaceable
                    and mutually beneficial conditions in the neighboring Central American
                    States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Theodore
                    Roosevelt.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
